traces/adsb-2026-11-05.jsonl.gz contains information from adsb.lol
(https://adsb.lol), made available under the Open Database License (ODbL)
v1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

It was recorded on 2026-11-05 from 18:17:41 to 19:17:41 UTC with

    gentrace -sensor a=39.0,-77.0,60 -sensor b=39.0,-76.2,60 -sensor c=39.0,-77.8,60 \
        -every 9s -duration 1h -out traces/adsb-2026-11-05.jsonl.gz

by polling the adsb.lol API for a 70 nm circle around 39.0,-77.0 once every
3 s and handing each response to the next sensor in turn. 601 of its 669
requests were answered and 68 failed, so sensors observe less often than
every 9 s. Each
line is a position report as one sensor received it: t_ms is when, relative
to the start of the recording, and delay_ms how long after the observation.

